<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προθύω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θύσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					805
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				548.11
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Berl.Sitzb.</u>
				1927.160
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θύσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			:—<i>sacrifice</i> or <i>offer first,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸ πάντων θεῶν τῇ Ἑστίᾳ πρώτῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					401d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ προμαντεύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					995
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>D</u>
				40
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>); <i>act as</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προθύτης,</span>
			<u>SIG</u>l.c.: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν θυγατέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.310d
				</span></i>
			:—more freq. in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ διὶ τὰ πέμματα</span>
			<i>take care that</i> they <i>are offered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3599.24
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Assos</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεθύετο ταῖς Μούσαις ὁ βασιλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).121.42
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				2.1651
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>to have</i> a person <i>sacrificed</i> or
				<i>slaughtered</i>
			
			<i>before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.19.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tox.</u>
				50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Charito
				7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				9.24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sacrifice for</i> or <i>in behalf of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					805
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ χθονὸς ἀρότου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			. (Both senses in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				38
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
